WEBVTT

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.510
My name is Emilio Langheim.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.530
I've come to speak with the leader of the Ignauts.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.950
Louise.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.620
I'm Demetrio of the Ignauts.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:30.890
So, what need brings the Prince of Endora to a place like this?

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.230
It's the King.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.890
I want your help in defeating Delzaine.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:56.980
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:07.050
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:17.440
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:27.440
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:37.620
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.140
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:58.140
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.810
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.970
"4: Ignauts"

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.240
I heard rumors about the Ignauts in the castle.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.550
They're a group of renegades who fight using guerrilla warfare...

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:36.550
...equal in strength to the Zoozian special forces that Delzaine employs, the Truculent.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.220
Oh? You think they're our equals, do you?

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.690
Someone's severely underestimating us.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:42.890
Right, Felix?

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.560
Let's kill them.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.500
After all, they've seen our faces now.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.670
Wait! Wait!

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.730
We won't turn you in!

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.040
I'll share with you everything
I know! So, please!

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.540
I'm not sure that I care.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.880
In all likelihood, we know everything this little prince has to share.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.550
He's useless.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.080
He'll say whatever it takes to be spared.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.050
No! I'm actually serious!

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:10.020
I've thrown everything away to kill Delzaine!

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.620
I'm not seeing it...

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.680
Why would you go that far to kill your own father?

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.400
Oh?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.530
What happened to all that vigor?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.740
This is a waste of time, Demetrio.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.740
Are we going to kill them, take them hostage, or what?

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.570
I don't like those options!

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:33.810
Silence.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.450
I need their strength...

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.780
Whatever it takes to bring him down...

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.650
I can't do it all on my own.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.660
Allow me to change the question.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.650
Supposing that you do kill the king, what then?

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.260
He hasn't even given it any thought.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.600
This is exactly why I hate spoiled princes.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:05.130
Answer me! What do you plan to do when the king is dead?!

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.680
I...

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.450
I don't care what happens, as long as he's dead.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.750
I'm ready to give up my life for it!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.290
You'll throw everything away, even your life?

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:33.530
You're not ready for anything!

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.930
I've heard my share of rumors, but this prince truly is daft.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.980
Delzaine must hate himself for raising such an incompetent son.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.020
Agreed?

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.680
You bastard!

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.200
What?! I didn't even see him summon anything!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.970
Of course not. That was no Warp Relic.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.840
Didn't think your Warp Relic could lose to a regular weapon?

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.220
You know, it's not always about what you have...

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.420
...it's about who has it.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.850
What are you saying?

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.160
Weapons, land, power...

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.890
They only matter as much as the one who wields them.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:33.260
Throwing everything away is the choice of a fool.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.870
So much for your plan!

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.400
Let's get out of here!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.280
Quit it! Let me down from here!

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:55.920
Hey!

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.390
--Put me down!
--Wait...

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.020
Stop ignoring me!

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:04.360
Are you saying if I want to kill the king,
I should be ready to take his place?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.030
Well, you could say that.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:11.400
However, I have no intention of helping you.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.470
If anyone brings down Delzaine, it'll be us, the Ignauts.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:18.530
There's no point in having a new king unless they have our backing.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:22.410
Then he'll prove it to you!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:29.080
He'll show you that he can be the kind of king you're looking for!

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.150
What's your name, boy?

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:34.710
Shun. Shun Asanaga.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:48.140
Around here, people don't go back on their word, Shun.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.270
Huh?

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:51.470
If you want to come, I won't stop you.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:56.310
But in return, you'll do everything I say.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.820
Good grief... And add these guys to our list of problems?

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:03.520
We've already got enough people swarming in to follow you.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.820
What will you do about rations?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.790
He who does not work, does not eat.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.160
We'll figure it out.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.830
Thank you.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.430
Don't get me wrong.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:17.930
If I decide you're not worthy to be king, you're on your own.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.470
But if I am?

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:24.170
If that day ever comes, I will be your sword.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:30.440
So show me what you've got, prince.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:45.560
Oho? Is this bread modeled after the DNA sequence of Endora frogs?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.560
This bread over here looks like ancient script.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.370
They're both just regular sweet buns.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.500
Is that so? You could have fooled me...

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.240
Oh well.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.970
It's good to see you.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:02.880
Isn't the army chasing you after your little prank?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.150
I reckon they didn't approve that I tampered with the Babel design.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:13.660
Yeah. They've been working day and night at the Royal Laboratory to fix the plans.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.830
It's a good thing our replacements are such hard workers.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.830
Us retired folk can sit back and rest assured.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:24.030
You're the one that made it easy for them to find.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:30.060
The Royal Laboratory would lose all dignity if they couldn't see through a senile old man's prank.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:37.240
I can't imagine you risked coming here just to check up on things.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:43.250
I've had many a suspicion ever since entering the Royal Laboratory.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.420
It's about that, eh?

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.190
And what if you knew?

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:50.630
I don't know, but if Babel is completed,

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.800
Endora and the surface will be reunited.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.470
I at least want to know before that happens.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:02.070
What does King Delzaine seek to accomplish by restoring Babel?

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:09.240
It's true that his determination to restore Babel borders on obsession...

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.980
...but unfortunately,
I don't have an answer for you.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.580
I see...

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.920
It's still too early to give up.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.490
Even with the plans complete, it will take time to restore Babel.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.290
In the meantime, I'll find out everything I can.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.960
Thank you.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.660
Think of it as a favor for an old colleague.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.600
Get me a new pot for baking bread and we'll call it even.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:33.270
I'll think about it.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:37.410
Is there any other news from the Royal Laboratory?

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.910
One of the young researchers was saying something.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.110
It was about those Warp Particles.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:45.010
Did they discover something?

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:50.150
They found that Endora's Warp Particles are decreasing year to year.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.650
I knew it...

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.520
But at the moment, it's just a local phenomenon.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:57.990
That's why only a select few know about it right now.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.930
What does it mean, though?

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.830
I'll have to look into that as well.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.800
By the way, you'll be interested to hear about the prince.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:12.040
Oh? You mean how Emilio ran away from the castle?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.840
I'm already well aware of that.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.280
To say he ran away would put it mildly.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.810
The prince is a wanted man now.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:23.150
After all, he tried to kill his father, the king.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.460
Position more scouts in the southern forest.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.030
Come on.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:40.570
Wait in here.

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:46.040
Dammit. How did we end up here?

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.380
Was this a part of your plan?

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.250
I told you not to do anything stupid.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.010
I'm the one that saved us!

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.320
Don't yell at me!

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:56.220
Shut up! You yelled at me first!

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.520
It's your fault this happened.

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:02.920
Think again! If it wasn't for me, you'd be dead by now!

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:07.230
I could have explained myself if we hadn't been ambushed.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.600
So these guys are revolutionaries?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.430
They seem pretty tough.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:14.770
That Demetrio doesn't even need a Warp Relic to kick ass.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:17.170
Enough. Don't you ever shut up?

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:20.540
I'm still pissed that your stupid plan failed.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.080
It did not fail!

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.570
You couldn't even answer his question!

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.290
Do you...

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.620
...really intend to kill your father?

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:37.230
Of course.

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:40.020
That's the only reason I push myself to live now.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.600
Out.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.790
Time for work. Come on.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:03.220
I wonder what revolutionaries do for work?

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:05.790
Go around and help people in need?

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:09.790
I know! Do they take money from the bad guys and give it to the poor?!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:10.960
It's gonna be sweet!

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.480
That's called a heroic outlaw.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.570
Laundry is heroic work, too.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:24.970
It's a bit different from what I thought, but hell, we're fresh recruits!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.810
I'm in! Let's do this!

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:32.580
What's this? Slacking on the job so soon?

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.620
What's the matter, prince?

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.450
He's never washed clothes in the river at the castle before.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.020
Here we take turns doing laundry and cooking.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:44.130
No exceptions for a prince.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:45.930
I get it.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:47.430
Even the boss does laundry?

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:48.960
Of course.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:52.700
I may be the figurehead of the Ignauts, but that doesn't make me special.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.600
Everyone is an equal comrade here.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:59.880
But you two are new, so listen to what the others say.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.510
Especially Shun.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.150
You're probably not used to life here in Endora yet.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:07.320
What? How did you know
I was from the surface?

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:08.820
You just told me.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:09.680
Idiot.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.620
No way! You tricked me!

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.560
Just make sure no one else finds out.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.060
People might come after you.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.660
All right.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.830
You don't seem at all surprised, Demetrio.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:23.570
All sorts of races make up
Endora and the Ignauts.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:27.800
What's it matter if we add one person from the surface to the mix?

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:28.800
Is that all?

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.510
That's all indeed.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.740
So get that laundry washed.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.640
He who does not work, does not eat.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.510
You hear that, prince?

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.050
Need me to show you how?

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:40.650
Stop calling me that!

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:43.050
I can do this well enough without your help!

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.700
Um...

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:00.440
Are you strong like everyone else, Eljuia?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.410
I just can't picture you swinging a weapon.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:06.840
No... I'm rather poor at fighting.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:10.540
That's why I pull my weight where I can.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:24.190
Huh? A dude?

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.190
You didn't notice?

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:28.560
You two have much to learn.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:31.300
Shut up! Is he all right?!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.700
This kinda thing happens all the time.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.970
Eljuia has the worst luck of anyone you'll ever see.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:41.880
He's always escaping death by a hair, though I guess that's lucky in itself.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.250
Eljuia? You okay?

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:49.890
Not so lucky...

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:51.290
Are you hurt?

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.420
Did you see it again?

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.330
Yes...

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.760
See what again?

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.160
The future.

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:03.130
He sees the future.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:07.070
Eljuia has possessed a special power since birth.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:13.340
When in a dangerous or emotional situation, he can glimpse into the future.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:14.680
You expect me to believe that?

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.340
That's so awesome!

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:21.920
Though, how unlucky is that--to be unable to control your own power?

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.490
What did you see?

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:26.790
What's it like? Come on, tell me!

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:27.860
Shun...

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.490
I saw your future.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.590
Huh?

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:34.100
It was a world I've never seen before.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.160
It may have been the surface.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:41.100
I saw you standing in an unknown world.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.040
Really? That's awesome!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.440
I'm going home! Woo-hoo!

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.980
What a spunky kid.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:49.510
Are you all right?

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.180
Your face still looks pale.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.670
I'm fine...

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.970
Emilio?

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:15.670
I'm back.

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.540
Oh... It's just Pascal.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.180
Just me? Ouch...

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.740
So, where are Shun and Emilio at?

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:26.210
When I woke up this morning, they were both missing!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.150
What? Don't tell me...

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:29.720
Don't tell you what?

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.750
Um...

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:36.210
Hey, Pascal? Did something happen between Emilio and Delzaine?

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:41.700
Why does he despise his father so much?

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:45.070
Well... Some people just don't get along with their parents.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:50.540
People should feel lucky to have parents, even if they can't get along...

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:53.210
So, where do you think they went?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:56.950
They probably headed towards
Babylon on their own.

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.010
We should hurry and catch up to them.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:00.410
Okay!

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.530
He says go that way!

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.930
Roger that!

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:20.100
Emilio! Shun! How could those guys leave me behind like that?!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.870
I'll make them pay for this!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.650
All done!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.550
You're getting too worked up for nothing.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.320
How can I relax knowing I get to go home?!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:42.290
I can't wait to eat my mom's cooking and sleep in my own bed...

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.790
You're a moron.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.430
You actually believe he can see the future?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:47.230
Huh?

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:49.330
It must be nice, having no brain.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.670
In just one day you believe everything they feed you.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.600
You're the one who wanted to meet these revolutionaries.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:57.970
Wasn't that because you trusted them?

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:01.110
I'm only using them to achieve my goal.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.180
So don't let your guard down.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.110
You're a pain in the ass.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:07.420
Don't you ever get tired of it?

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.790
You'll be best pals with anyone without even thinking twice!

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:13.520
I trust my gut and it's never let me down.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.120
Sure, I was a bit scared at first...

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.090
But you know, I'm starting to like these guys.

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:22.160
If you trust everyone that easily, you're bound to get hurt.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.700
You never know what their true intentions are...

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.340
With an attitude like that, there's no use in trusting anybody.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.770
Don't you dare try to lecture me!

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.280
What the hell?

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.280
Why are you in such a bad mood?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:39.710
Oh. Will you be lonely if I go back to the surface?

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:40.950
Don't make me laugh.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:44.050
It'll be a load off my shoulders when you're gone.

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:46.450
That is, if you ever do get home.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.160
Is that any way to talk to the person helping you?

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.830
And to think I came along for you...

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:52.990
Leave. See if I care.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:56.900
Go back to the surface and cry to your mother.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.370
You really are a despicable person.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.670
Are all princes as smug as you?

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.340
You're so full of yourself!

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:05.970
That's why no one wants to help you!

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:08.140
You're nothing like Demetrio!

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:13.880
What do you know about me...?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:19.320
I don't want to know anything about a monster who tries to kill his parents!

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.720
You bastard!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.660
You asked for it!

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.960
Son of a--

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.240
So it has begun...

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.100
You aren't going to stop them?

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.740
They're just a couple brats having a fight.

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:15.230
They'll come back when they're hungry.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.750
They say it's people who fight...

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.610
...who get along best?

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:22.150
Though I'm not so sure in this case.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.720
Is this how men talk--with their fists?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.120
That's so stupid.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.930
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:09.700
<i>Took a long way to get here</i>

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.670
<i>Had to go around and around</i>

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:17.810
<i>But every single road I've taken</i>

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:21.680
<i>Made me who I am today</i>

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:28.640
<i>go my way go my way</i>

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:40.130
<i>The world will show you there's tomorrow</i>

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:48.660
<i>Look up to the blue sky and you will see</i>

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:57.550
<i>I try to be better than who I was yesterday</i>

00:21:57.550 --> 00:22:04.720
<i>So I can see you with a smile on my face today</i>

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:09.990
<i>Now what should we get into today?</i>

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:18.600
<i>The scent of summer arouses my heart</i>

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.740
<i>And I can't seem to find the right words to tell you</i>

00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:28.200
<i>That I love you just the way you are</i>

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:39.940
"Episode 5: Assault"

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.920
Next episode, "Assault."
